        "content": "<p>Hi! I'd like to know whether mathlib would want the complex (and real) Lambert W function (the branchwise inverse of <code>z ↦ z * exp z</code> on <code>ℂ</code>).</p>\n<p>There was an earlier discussion in \"Is there code for X?\" <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Lambert.20W.20function.20.26.20sinc.20integral\">here</a>.</p>\n<p>I currently plan to define <code>Complex.lambertW : ℤ -&gt; ℂ -&gt; ℂ</code> as follows</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- below is a draft</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Complex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeBelowAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">im</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">η</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">private</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeAboveAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Ioo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">cot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">η</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">im</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">η</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Int</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRange</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ofNat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeBelowAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeAboveAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeBelowAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">im</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeAboveAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeBelowAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeAboveAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeAboveAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">im</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≤</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeBelowAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"bp\">_+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeAboveAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRangeBelowAux</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Complex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lambertW</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Function</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">invFunOn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Complex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">exp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">lambertWRange</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lambertWZero</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Complex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lambertW</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lambertWNegOne</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Complex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">lambertW</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">re</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- noncomputable def Real.Omega : ℝ := Real.lambertWZero 1 -- A030178</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The branch cut of <code>W₀</code> is <code>(-∞, -1 / e]</code>, while the branch cut for other branches is <code>(-∞, 0]</code><br>\nFor <code>k ≠ 0</code>, <code>Complex.lambertW k 0</code> will be the junk value from <code>Function.invFunOn</code>.<br>\nThe boundary choice for the range of <code>Wₖ</code> follows the rule of <em>counter-clockwise continuity</em>. This should be the standard choice used by Mathematica and Maple.</p>\n<p>I'd like to prove some basic properties of <code>W</code>, like some special values, continuity, differentiability, smoothness, etc.</p>\n<p>Would this be a good fit for mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 621729913,
        "sender_full_name": "Emlis",
        "timestamp": 1788532769
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are we sure that this is the best way to do branch cuts in Mathlib? It would be nice to develop a general API for this sort of thing. For Complex Analysis, will need certainly need arbitrary branch cuts for <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.log#doc\">docs#Complex.log</a> or <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.sqrt#doc\">docs#Complex.sqrt</a>.</p>",
        "id": 621796337,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1788550543
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Also, perhaps we should consider this <a href=\"https://ckms.kms.or.kr/journal/view.html?doi=10.4134%2FCKMS.c250146\">generalization</a> of the W function?</p>",
        "id": 621818911,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1788558806
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There are a number of different generalizations of the W function (essentially all making some modification to the equation it's suppose to invert), and they can't all be captured at once in a useful way, so I think just getting the standard one is the most reasonable thing. If anyone feels the need for a generalization it can always be done later. This is not the same scenario as \"generalize to n dimensions and then put n =  1 for the special case\", since there isn't any clearly better or all-encompassing generalization</p>",
        "id": 621879352,
        "sender_full_name": "Luigi Massacci",
        "timestamp": 1788596379
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>as for branch cuts, someone who uses the complex analysis part of the library more than me should weigh in, but just as coming up with a general approach to branch cuts in mathlib wasn't a pre-requisite to getting <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.log#doc\">docs#Complex.log</a>, it doesn't seem necessary to me that it should stop the W function. For the W function specifically my understanding is those are standard and mathematically nice choices, and lean-wise it seems good to me</p>",
        "id": 621879670,
        "sender_full_name": "Luigi Massacci",
        "timestamp": 1788596600
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"918641\">@Emlis</span> if you do PR it (or hopefully <em>when</em>), you can <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Tactic/CrossRefAttribute.html#Cross-reference-attributes\">cross-reference the entries</a> for the W function in the DLMF if you want</p>",
        "id": 621879989,
        "sender_full_name": "Luigi Massacci",
        "timestamp": 1788596846
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for the feedback!</p>\n<p>Regarding the general branch cut API, I don't have a clear idea of how to do that properly right now, so I'd rather not block on it. I plan to submit the standard Lambert W function first. I won't attempt the general branch cut framework myself, but if one lands later, I'd be happy to adapt that. I'll do the cross-reference thing, thanks!</p>",
        "id": 621918347,
        "sender_full_name": "Emlis",
        "timestamp": 1788621121
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.log#doc\">docs#Complex.log</a> and <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.sqrt#doc\">docs#Complex.sqrt</a>, it is pretty easy to move between branches by adding a term to the expression, so the demand for a better branch cut API there is probably less. I don't know enough about Lambert W function to say whether this is true for it</p>",
        "id": 621918927,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1788621375
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873350\">Weiyi Wang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/adding.20the.20Complex.20LambertW.20function/near/621918927\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>it is pretty easy to move between branches by adding a term to the expression</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Well, yes and no. For <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.log#doc\">docs#Complex.log</a> in particular, the branch cut is defined along the <del>positive</del> negative real axis. Adding a constant offset rotates the ray, but it will always be along a straight line unless you get really fancy. </p>\n<p>In principle, we should be able to define the logarithm on any simply connected domain of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{C}^*</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, and there are cases in complex analysis where one requires these more subtle branch cuts. From the Riemann surface point-of-view, what we'd really like to say is that <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.exp#doc\">docs#Complex.exp</a> is the universal covering map of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">C</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathbb{C}^*</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbb\">C</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6887em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mbin mtight\">∗</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span>, and a \"branch cut\" is actually just any choice of an evenly-covered subset--on which <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.log#doc\">docs#Complex.log</a> is then the holomorphic section.</p>",
        "id": 622135477,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1788736121
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I agree we shouldn't block on this, but just wanted to point out that this definition of LambertW will probably need to get refactored in the future when we figure out how to multivalued/branched functions \"properly\" in Mathlib</p>",
        "id": 622135801,
        "sender_full_name": "Jack McCarthy",
        "timestamp": 1788736273
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"989743\">Jack McCarthy</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/adding.20the.20Complex.20LambertW.20function/near/622135477\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>For <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Complex.log#doc\">docs#Complex.log</a> in particular, the branch cut is defined along the positive real axis.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Negative, no?</p>",
        "id": 622137962,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1788737495
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I've opened a PR for the standard complex Lambert W function (<a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43811\">#43811</a>).</p>\n<p>It currently defines the domains, and ranges, defines <code>Complex.lambertW : ℤ → ℂ → ℂ</code> as the inverse of <code>w =&gt; w * exp w</code> on each branch range, and proves the basic bijection and inverse properties. It also includes the existence of a branch for every solution of <code>z = w * exp w</code>, as well as uniqueness of the branch when <code>w ≠ -1</code>.</p>\n<p>I didn't use the previous <code>lambertWRange{Below, Above}Aux</code> version definition of ranges, since that version wasn't convenient to work with. Instead, I now defines ranges using <code>w.arg + w.im ∈ Ioc ((2 * k ± 1) * π)</code>.</p>\n<p>Later I'm going to define Lambert W on <code>ℝ</code> as well in a subsequent PR.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"c1\">-- the new range definition</span>\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">expose</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">range</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">match</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">im</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">\\</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Iio</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">im</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">3</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∪</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Iic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">×</span><span class=\"n\">ℂ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">arg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">im</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Ioc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">((</span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">π</span><span class=\"o\">)}</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 624172780,
        "sender_full_name": "Emlis",
        "timestamp": 1789417350
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oof, that's quite a long file to get the definition. As I said I was not familiar with the topic, but the length interested me and I might take this chance to learn a bit...</p>",
        "id": 624678884,
        "sender_full_name": "Weiyi Wang",
        "timestamp": 1789571677
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks for taking a look! As noted in the implementation notes, most of the length is in solving the polar form of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><msup><mi>e</mi><mi>w</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">w e ^ w = z</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">e</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6644em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.4306em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.044em;\">z</span></span></span></span>, and in working through seven cases. If there is a more elegant proof of the bijectivity in Lean, I would be glad to hear it.</p>",
        "id": 624696780,
        "sender_full_name": "Emlis",
        "timestamp": 1789575473
    }
]